  <ferc:DisclosureOfPurchaseOrSaleOfAnOperatingUnitOrSystemTextBlock id="HHB507706EE223692FB3CE9DE4D62FC621" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;3. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfPurchaseOrSaleOfAnOperatingUnitOrSystemTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantLeaseholdsThatHaveBeenAcquiredOrGivenAssignedOrSurrenderedTextBlock id="HH1C967D5CB7055C23C61684D3A8ADDA65" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNoSpacing"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;4. In March 2026, Tampa Electric entered into an operating lessor lease agreement with SSA BIG BEND TERMINAL, LLC commencing on March 1, 2026, through February 2036, with two options to extend, each consisting of ten lease years. The total fixed lease revenue is approximately $34 million.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantLeaseholdsThatHaveBeenAcquiredOrGivenAssignedOrSurrenderedTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantExtensionOrReductionOfTransmissionOrDistributionSystemTextBlock id="HH3753C2D0F64441EEC1CB77241E2239DC" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;5. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantExtensionOrReductionOfTransmissionOrDistributionSystemTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock id="HH2FB9527C1D4BB25D79F1C0C76F5BC95D" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;6.&amp;#160; Tampa Electric Company (&amp;#8220;the Company&amp;#8221;) has authorization to issue and sell securities as approved in the Florida Public Service Commission Order No. PSC- 2022-0363-FOF-PU dated October 25, 2022.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;The Company borrows under its revolving credit facility and commercial paper program, which permits the Company to draw down, repay, and re-borrow funds. Given the frequency of these borrowings and repayments, it is not practicable to give the details of each action. However, the Company&amp;#8217;s borrowing activity in Q1 2026 can be summarized as follows:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNoSpacing"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;($ Millions)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNoSpacing"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;Minimum Outstanding $641&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNoSpacing"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;Maximum Outstanding $ 853&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNoSpacing"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;Average Outstanding $ 750&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNoSpacing"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;Weighted Average Interest Cost 3.92%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock id="HHDB4E63D65FD21AE5462A8FBA840EA717" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;7. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock id="HHEBA1CD44839C108D1DAFD6DE3427BE45" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;8. The Union contracts cover 736 active employees represented by the International Brotherhood of Electrical Workers and 128 active employees represented by the Office and Professional Employees International Union as of March 31, 2026, at Tampa Electric Company. In 2026, the OPEIU and IBEW contracts provided for base wage increases of 3.25% and 3.85% respectively&lt;span class="ui-provider"&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;Employees not represented by a union are eligible for annual merit review. The annual merit budget for 2025 performance year was 3.75%, and annual merit increases went into effect on January 1, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock id="HH22FBAEA0509E80B804A4341B1670898A" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;9. See note 8 in the Notes to Financial Statements on page 122 for the status and results of materially important legal proceedings.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock>
